Saudi Arabia's Crown Prince says his  country will develop a nuclear bomb if  Iran builds nuclear weapons Mohammed bin  Salman made that startling statement  during our recent visit to Saudi Arabia  for this Sunday's 60 minutes it is the  first u.s. television interview with a  Saudi leader since 2005 and we asked the  32 year old Crown Prince about the  political economic and social reforms  unfolding in the kingdom  we also discussed foreign policy in  Saudi Arabia's longtime foe Iran you've  been rivals for centuries  at its heart what is this rift about is  it a battle for Islam is it  Iran is not a rival to Saudi Arabia it's  army is not among the top five armies in  the Muslim world the Saudi economy is  larger than the Iranian economy Iran is  far from being equal to Saudi Arabia but  I've seen that you called the Ayatollah  Khamenei the new Hitler of the Middle  East leadership absolutely why because  he wants to expand he wants to create  his own project in the Middle East very  much like Hitler who wanted to expand at  the time many countries around the world  and in Europe did not realize how  dangerous Hitler was until what happened  happened I don't want to see the same  events happening in the Middle East does  Saudi Arabia need nuclear weapons to  counter Iran Saudi Arabia does not want  to acquire any nuclear bomb but without  a doubt if Iran developed a nuclear bomb  we will follow suit as soon as possible  and you can see our full report with the  Saudi Crown Prince Sunday night on 60  minutes right here on CBS
 

